WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.900
The AI gateway that holds

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.281
your model keys is under

00:00:03.081 --> 00:00:05.007
attack, for the fourth time

00:00:04.807 --> 00:00:05.559
this year.

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:07.856
The fix is one upgrade.

00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:09.939
Version one point eight four

00:00:09.739 --> 00:00:11.628
point zero or later clears

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:12.549
all four holes.

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:15.260
A guardrail tester runs Python

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:15.914
you send it.

00:00:15.954 --> 00:00:17.841
Its sandbox only scanned the

00:00:17.641 --> 00:00:19.880
text, so clever code walked past.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.747
In the default Docker image,

00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:22.561
that means root.

00:00:23.111 --> 00:00:24.717
It needs an admin key,

00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:26.335
so the maintainers rated it

00:00:26.135 --> 00:00:27.249
five point nine.

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:29.866
Public databases say eight point eight.

00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:32.435
In May, an SQL injection

00:00:32.235 --> 00:00:33.510
needed no login.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.456
In June, command injection.

00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:37.289
In September, any made up

00:00:37.089 --> 00:00:38.051
token worked.

00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:39.831
Now, the guardrail tester.

00:00:40.381 --> 00:00:42.377
Nothing public ties these into

00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:43.137
one campaign.

00:00:43.177 --> 00:00:44.868
But an attacker may already

00:00:44.668 --> 00:00:46.359
hold a leaked admin key,

00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:47.462
and with this bug,

00:00:47.262 --> 00:00:48.110
that is root.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.393
Find every copy you run.

00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:52.038
Upgrade to one point eight

00:00:51.838 --> 00:00:52.740
four or later.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.932
If you cannot,

00:00:53.732 --> 00:00:55.427
block the risky test paths

00:00:55.227 --> 00:00:56.650
at your reverse proxy.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.353
Put the admin interface behind

00:00:59.153 --> 00:00:59.728
a VPN.

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:01.238
If you were exposed,

00:01:01.038 --> 00:01:02.708
rotate every key the proxy

00:01:02.508 --> 00:01:04.312
holds and check your billing.

00:01:04.862 --> 00:01:07.028
These gateways hold every model

00:01:06.828 --> 00:01:08.484
key and see every prompt.

00:01:08.524 --> 00:01:10.520
Treat yours like a password vault.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.483
The paths to block are

00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:13.561
in the full story on

00:01:13.361 --> 00:01:14.302
The Dispatch.

